{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "17", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "11", "M": "48", "S": "22"}}, "news": [{"title": "Building around heritage, not over it: A new approach to urban development in India\u2019s historic cities", "para": "Historic cities stand at a crossroads where preservation meets modern progress, requiring thoughtful integration of contemporary architecture alongside traditional landscapes. Ensuring sustainability and honoring local customs can significantly improve urban life. Developers are encouraged to assess how new structures will affect neighboring communities and shared spaces, fostering an environment where a robust economy flourishes in harmony with cultural heritage.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/blog/building-around-heritage-not-over-it-a-new-approach-to-urban-development-in-indias-historic-cities/135013104?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-188328/135013104.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "building-around-heritage-not-over-it-a-new-approach-to-urban-development-in-indias-historic-cities"}, {"title": "Protected tenancy in Telangana: Why due diligence must go beyond sale deeds & encumbrance searches", "para": "The land tenure system in Telangana has deep roots in historical land distribution inequities and laws enacted after Independence. The Telangana Tenancy and Agricultural Lands Act of 1950 establishes tenant rights, which can complicate current ownership claims. Protected tenants hold significant rights, including the right of first offer for purchase.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/blog/protected-tenancy-in-telangana-why-due-diligence-must-go-beyond-sale-deeds-encumbrance-searches/135012978?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-122530/135012978.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "protected-tenancy-in-telangana-why-due-diligence-must-go-beyond-sale-deeds-encumbrance-searches"}, {"title": "Private equity investment in Indian real estate rises 16% to $4.5 billion in Jan-Sep 2026", "para": "Private equity inflows into Indian real estate increased 16% year-on-year to $4.5 billion during January-September 2026. Q3 inflows stood at $1.3 billion, with hospitality accounting for the largest share of quarterly investments at 26%.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/private-equity-investment-in-indian-real-estate-rises-16-to-4-5-billion-in-jan-sep-2026/135007157?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-298820/135007157.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}